#N canvas 0 0 760 700 10;
#X text 12 8 nsf~ - NSF/NSFE player (6502 engine + frame timing) -> nes~;
#X text 12 28 nsf~ owns the file and the 6502 CPU and streams every APU register write as `nes <reg> <val>` on outlet 0 - connect it straight to nes~ (same playback/generation split as vgm~ -> opl3~/nes~). Outlet 1 = the DPCM channel as a signal (sample data cannot ride register messages - the vgm~ DAC precedent\; AC-coupled \, so idle DAC levels fade out instead of clicking). Outlet 2 = end bang (NSFE play lengths \, loop off);
#X text 12 98 messages (the vgm~ set): load <file> \, play \, pause \, stop \, goto <track 1..n> \, loop <0/1> \, info. Pause = halt + all channels off\; play resumes by re-initializing the track (the engine owns its register state). Expansion chips (VRC6/FDS/MMC5/N163/5B/VRC7) are NOT emulated - the load line says so and the 2A03 channels still play;
#X msg 20 250 load demo_nes.nsf;
#X msg 20 280 play;
#X msg 20 310 stop;
#X msg 20 340 info;
#X msg 140 250 goto 1;
#X msg 140 280 loop 1;
#X msg 140 310 loop 0;
#X text 240 250 goto = track select (1-based) + re-init;
#X obj 20 400 nsf~;
#X obj 20 460 nes~;
#X obj 20 520 *~ 0.5;
#X obj 20 560 dac~;
#X obj 20 600 graph~ 200 90;
#X text 240 600 nes~ ch1 (pulse 1) scope - wire 2..5 for the rest;
#X text 12 650 pure 2A03 files play fully\; NSFE time chunks drive the end bang when loop is 0;
#X text 240 340 mode <single/seqloop/seqstop/randloop/randstop> = what a track end does (advance modes need a length: NSFE time chunks \, else songtime);
#X msg 140 340 mode seqloop;
#X msg 140 370 mode randstop;
#X msg 140 400 mode single;
#X msg 240 370 songtime 45;
#X text 380 370 default per-track length for files without NSFE times (default 120 s);
#X connect 3 0 11 0;
#X connect 4 0 11 0;
#X connect 5 0 11 0;
#X connect 6 0 11 0;
#X connect 7 0 11 0;
#X connect 8 0 11 0;
#X connect 9 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X connect 12 0 13 0;
#X connect 13 0 14 0;
#X connect 13 0 14 1;
#X connect 12 1 15 0;
#X connect 19 0 11 0;
#X connect 20 0 11 0;
#X connect 21 0 11 0;
#X connect 22 0 11 0;
